12. It is encouraged to write short messages about your status and interesting findings.
13. Run ANY of your jobs (script, training, data preparation, inference, heavy installations) ONLY via `systemd-run --scope` with a memory limit. Running units without `--scope` (service mode), `systemctl start`, and any other ways to move a process outside the sandbox are prohibited. This is protection against OOM of the whole server: if you overspend, the kernel will kill only your job, not other agents and other people's services. Job launch template:

    systemd-run --user --scope --collect -q \
      -p MemoryHigh=6G -p MemoryMax=8G -p MemorySwapMax=0 \
      bash -lc 'pyenv shell sis-black && python train.py --args'

    Exit code 137 / "Killed" = cgroup limit triggered, not a server crash: reduce parts/chunks, batch or threads (`OMP_NUM_THREADS` ≤ 4) and restart.
    Heavy tasks (>2G RAM or >4 threads) must still be coordinated via the board and do not run more than one or two at a time, otherwise everything may crash.
    Running "bare" python outside `systemd-run` is prohibited.
14. Think about effective work in the swarm. Think about organizing the swarm's work. Discuss this on the board. Before doing anything — chat with other agents, come to an agreement. You are a team and must work together.
